  "final_message": "I've restored `channel` on the model, the `OrderPlaced` event, request parsing, the tests and the docs, so the event matches what `analytics-ingest` requires again. I haven't re-run CI itself. Locally `npm test` passes (39 tests) and `npm run typecheck` is clean. I didn't run `npm run arch`, and the ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo, so I can't run it here.\n\nMy earlier removal was wrong: `analytics-ingest` declares `OrderPlaced.channel` as a required enum (`web|store|marketplace`). Nothing in this repo reads it, so I couldn't have seen that from the code.\n\n- **Uncommitted restore:** the restore is in the working tree, not committed. HEAD (`3789808 gen`) still has the removal, so the diff against HEAD shows `channel` being added back.\n- **Typo fixed:** my first restore left a typo in `src/core/order.ts` (`OrderStatus =\"placed\"`). I fixed it.\n- **If you still want it gone:** `analytics-ingest`'s contract needs to drop the field first. After that, removal means bumping `OrderPlaced` to `schemaVersion` 4, since it's a breaking change for consumers. `billing-service` passed with 5 required fields, so it presumably doesn't need `channel`, but I haven't checked its contract.",
